' The C64 one-liner, as one line and without a loop.
'
' The original was 10 PRINT CHR$(205.5+RND(1)); : GOTO 10 - two diagonal
' characters picked at random, filling the screen with a maze nobody
' designed. Here the loop is gone entirely: RND runs over an array, CHR$
' runs over its result, and JOIN glues the lot into one string. The
' diagonals sit at 215 and 216 in this font.
'
' The count is what the board's memory allows, not what the screen holds:
' every character is an array element on the way there.

PRINT JOIN(CHR$(215 + INT(RND(IOTA(800, 0)) * 2)), "");
